course: dictionary
lesson: 10326
title: Traffic: one word, more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. You can tell which meaning the writer wants by reading the words around it. This is context. «Traffic» is a good example: it can mean the cars and buses on the road, or the movement of planes, ships or data.
explain: Read this: «In the USA and Canada traffic drives on the right, so you look left first.» Here traffic means vehicles on the road, because the words drives and look tell you that. If the sentence were about ships, you would not need to look for cars at all.
explain: Road safety uses this word a lot. «Drive a remote-control car only in the yard, park or a quiet path, never in the street, because you might run after it into traffic.» Traffic means the cars and other vehicles, so the danger is clear.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. Try «into cars» in place of «into traffic»: it still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: «Traffic» means the cars, buses, lorries, bikes and other vehicles moving on roads.
fact: «Traffic» can also mean the movement of people, ships, planes or data, as in «air traffic» and «internet traffic».
fact: In the UK, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand traffic drives on the left. In the USA and Canada it drives on the right.
fact: Useful phrases are traffic lights, traffic jam, heavy traffic, oncoming traffic and rush-hour traffic.
fact: A traffic jam can make people late, and a bus stuck in traffic can still show «due» on a bus stop sign.
exercise: «Route-finding algorithms compare many possible roads, add up the time for each, and pick the shortest total; map apps also use traffic reports.» What does traffic mean here? | *Cars and other vehicles moving on the roads | People walking in a park | Only the cars in one car park | Illegal buying and selling
exercise: In the UK, which way does traffic drive? | On the right | It does not move | *On the left | Straight up
exercise: Lena says «air traffic» means cars in the sky. What does air traffic really mean? | *Planes moving through the air | Birds flying in a flock | Clouds moving in the wind | Cars in the sky
test: «The bus was stuck in heavy traffic.» What does heavy traffic mean? | Light rain | Very loud music | *Lots of vehicles moving slowly or stopped | Sunny weather
test: Which phrase means a long line of stopped cars? | Traffic warden | Traffic light | *Traffic jam | Traffic cone
exam: Mo says «traffic» always means cars on a road. Is he right? | *No, traffic can also mean the movement of planes, ships or data | No, traffic means only buses | Yes, always | Yes, but only in the USA
